Fix the XForms public header include path for the packaged libforms layout

xcolmix 1.07 (1996) is written against the X11R6-era XForms install layout,
where the generated public header was reachable as <X11/forms.h>; upstream's
own ChangeLog entry for 1.07 records that move ("design.c and xcolmix.h now
have #include <X11/forms.h>").

The libforms/1.2.4 Conan package installs the build-generated header as
<libforms-prefix>/include/forms.h and has no include/X11/ directory, so the
two translation units that pull in the public header have to spell it
<forms.h>.  This is a pure include-path adaptation: no platform macro is
involved, the same header is found, and it still reaches <X11/Xlib.h> through
libforms' own include chain.

diff --git a/src/design.c b/src/design.c
index 44b3113..e6007eb 100644
--- a/src/design.c
+++ b/src/design.c
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@
 /* <<< End of information >>>                                               */
 /* Form definition file generated with fdesign. */
 
-#include <X11/forms.h>
+#include <forms.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include "design.h"
 
diff --git a/src/xcolmix.h b/src/xcolmix.h
index 91e4085..b082904 100644
--- a/src/xcolmix.h
+++ b/src/xcolmix.h
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@
 /* Foundation, Inc., 59 Temple Place, Suite 330, Boston, MA  02111-1307 USA */
 /* <<< End of information >>>                                               */
 
-#include <X11/forms.h>
+#include <forms.h>
 #include <malloc.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <unistd.h> 
